# Supported browsers.
#
# Lion needs the native modal dialog. A modal overlay is opened with `<dialog>.showModal()`, and from
# then on the platform is what keeps the keyboard focus inside the dialog and makes the rest of the page
# unreachable - which is also why a screen reader does not read that other content. There is no fallback
# for a browser that cannot do this, because the same two effects cannot be re-created reliably without
# the top layer of the browser. IE11 and Safari 15 and older are therefore not supported: the oldest
# supported browser is Safari 16.
safari >= 16
ios_saf >= 16
last 4 Chrome versions
last 4 Edge versions
last 4 Firefox versions
